# Documentation

When you add or change behaviour, update the matching docs in the same change.

- `README.md` — purpose, run commands, env vars, current MCP tools, limits.
- `AGENTS.md` — agent-facing conventions (this file’s siblings, Linear, secrets).
- Code comments — non-obvious API quirks only (auth, confirm gates, schema merge).
- Do not leave README tool lists or env tables out of date.

There is no live LawPracticeZA access until credentials exist. Say so wherever a reader might assume live calls.
